{"id": "z0819", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The answer is crash. If an airplane's engine s cut off and can't be restarted, the plane loses critical power for lift and control. Without engine thrust or enough speed to stay aloft, it will inevitably descend rapidly. Pilots are trained to manage emergency situations, but without working engine s, they usually cannot safely recover, especially at high altitudes or low speeds. So a crash is the likely outcome if engines fail completely and cannot be restarted in flight.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 26, "carrier_ended": null}
