{"id": "z0835", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "After killing people, the murder er went to church after feeling B: remor se. This is the most logical answer because remorse describes the deep regret or guilt a person feels after doing something terrible like kill ing someone. Going to church is often seen as an attempt to seek forgiveness or find peace when someone is overwhelmed by guilt. While other options like anguish might also fit, remorse directly connects the act of murder with the emotional state that lead s someone to try to make amends through religion.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 27, "carrier_ended": null}
