{"id": "z0867", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The most likely place for a child to sit at a desk is B, school room. Desk s are commonly found in schoolrooms where children go to learn and do their homework. While furniture stores sell desks, they aren't places where kids typically sit at them. Pa ttio s and office buildings usually don't have the right setup for children's daily activities. Lib raries might have desks, but school rooms are more directly associated with children using desks regularly.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
