{"id": "z1131", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The life work of a flower is to be successfully fertilized. That's its main purpose. While the other options like providing nice scents, looking pretty, or growing tall are helpful in attract ing pollinators, the ultimate goal is reproduction through successful fertilization.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 17, "carrier_ended": null}
