{"id": "z1147", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "As water levels rise, beaches shrink. The higher water er odes the sand and sediment that form beach es, causing them to become narrower or disappear altogether.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1155", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "To change an object's shape, the correct answer is A. Ri p off a corner portion. This directly alters its form by removing part of it. Lay ing it flat or coloring the edges doesn't change its shape, and adding tape might slightly alter it but not as effectively as removing material.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
