{"id": "z1179", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 18, "onset_chunk": 17, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The steam is water vapor. When you take the pot off the stove, the hot water turns into gas form and rises up as invisible steam. So it's definitely not cold air or dry, because it comes from boiling water. It also isn't liquid boil ing water anymore since it's already turned to gas.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1187", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A moth leaving its cocoon is the final step in a life cycle. Moths undergo complete metamorphosis, which includes four stages egg, larva, pupa, and adult. The co coon stage represents the pupa phase where transformation occurs. When the moth emerges from the cocoon, it has fully developed into an adult moth, completing its life cycle. While trans formation happens during the pupa stage, leaving the cocoon marks the end of that process and the beginning of the adult phase. So the correct answer is A, life cycle.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 26, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1195", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Pine needles can be used as biofuel.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1203", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Owls are likely to hunt at D, 7 AM. Most owl species are nocturnal or crepus cular, meaning they are most active during the night or at dawn and dusk. While some might hunt later in the evening, early morning hunting aligns with their natural activity pe aks as prey becomes more active.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1211", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Beak shape can influence a bird's ability to chew up certain worms. The beak is specifically adapted for different types of food, and worm- eating birds often have beaks that are strong enough to grip and tear into soil or mud where worms live. So the correct answer is D: to chew up certain worms.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1219", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "It could be a magnetized compass.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 2, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1227", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The reason Earth is so sturdy is because A, it is made from rock. While the Earth' s core is mostly metal, its crust and mantle are primarily composed of rock. This combination gives the planet its structural strength and stability. Options B and C are not accurate, as planets do not eat or have families in the way living organisms do.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
