{"id": "z1267", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is B, kittens look like their parents. This shows that fur color ation is inherited from the parents. P uppies having soft fur doesn' t show inheritance of color. All ma mmals having fur isn' t specific to color. Baby rats being bald doesn't relate to fur color either.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 17, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1275", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A light was off because the cord was sitting on the table. When a light isn't working, it' s often because the power source isn't connected or properly in place. If the cord is just lying around and not plugged in, that's why the light doesn't work. The other options like being attached to the wall or an extension cord would usually mean the light should be on if everything else works. So the most likely reason is that the cord is just sitting there, unplug ged.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
