{"id": "z1299", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Water can turn to vapor when boil ing eggs on a stovetop. That is option C. When you heat water enough for it to boil, the liquid turns into gas, which we call steam or vapor. The other options are not correct because putting water on an off stove burner won ’t make it hot enough to turn into vapor. Pl acing it in a freeze r makes it cold and solid, like ice. And room temperature doesn ’t provide enough heat for vaporization either. So, the right answer is C, boil ing eggs on a stove top.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 27, "carrier_ended": null}
