{"id": "z1867", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 20, "onset_chunk": 19, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "330 students suggested ma shed potatoes and 2 6 9 suggested bacon. So, to find how many more students suggested mashed potatoes than bacon, I subtract the number of students who suggested bacon from those who suggested ma shed potatoes: 3 30 minus 26 9 equals 6 1. So, 61 more students suggested ma shed potatoes than bacon.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 23, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1875", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So, if Ed had 10 more marbles than Doug originally, and he had 4 5 marbles, that means Doug started with 35. Then Doug lost 11 at the playground, leaving him with 24. So, now Ed has 45 and Doug has 24, which means Ed has 2 1 more marble s than Doug.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1883", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "To find the total number of students, you multi ply the number of grade s by the number of students in each grade. So that's 3 04 grades times 75 students per grade. Let' s break it down: First, multiply 3 00 by 75, which gives 22 500, then add 4 times 7 5, which is 3 00. Adding those together, 2 25 00 plus 3 00 equals 2 280 0. So there were 22 800 students in total.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 26, "carrier_ended": null}
