{"id": "z1907", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 18, "onset_chunk": 17, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is D, unauthorized network access. While this can be a security concern in general, it's not specifically classified as a transport layer vulnerability. Transport layer issues typically involve things like mismanaging variables or overloading mechanisms within that layer itself. So options A, B, and C are more directly related to the challenges of the transport layer.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1915", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The Federal Open Market Committee, or F OMC, is part of the Federal Reserve System. It advises the president on monetary policy but does not directly advise him. It has more than seven members and its main role is to manage interest rates and money supply, not to promote free trade. So the correct answer is B: it is part of the Federal Re serve System.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 21, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1923", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 28, "onset_chunk": 27, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Let's go through this step by step. We're given a ring R with a multi plicative identity, and U is an add itive subgroup of R such that for any u in U and r in R, both ur and ru are in U. That means U is a two- sided ideal. But the question says \" right ideal,\" so we' ll assume it's referring to right ideals only, meaning for all u in U and r in R, ur is in U. Now, if R has exactly two right ideals, what does that tell us? One of them must be the zero ideal, which always exists. The other one must be the entire ring R itself. Why? Because if there were any other proper right ideal between zero and R, then we'd have more than two ideals. So the only possibilities are {0} and R. This structure is characteristic of division ring s. In a division ring, every non- zero element has a multiplicative inverse, and the only right ideals are the zero ideal and the whole ring. So statement 2 must be true. What about statement 1? Is R commutative? Not necessarily. A division ring doesn't have to be commutative; for example, the qua ternions form a division ring but aren't commutative. So I is not required. Statement 3: R is infinite. Well, a", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 60, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1931", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 20, "onset_chunk": 19, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Okay, let's think about this. So home o tic cluster genes are basically the master switch es for body plan formation in Drosophila. If you mess with them, you get segment al defects. Now looking at the options: A says absence of a group of segments—that sounds like a big missing piece. B is transformation between segments— that' s more like a segment identity issue. C talks about polarity along the anterior-posterior axis, which is more related to gap genes or pair rule genes. And D is tumor s in imaginal disc s—that usually comes from oncogenes or tumor suppressors. So if I recall correctly, when you mutate home otic cluster genes, you often see that whole groups of segments are missing because the entire region isn't being specified properly. That makes me think A is the right answer.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 42, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1939", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 31, "onset_chunk": 27, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So, a. Realists argue that states will protect their own citizens and are unlikely to rely on outside intervention for protection. This is one of the main criticisms of humanitarian intervention from a realist perspective. B. While sovereignty does involve responsibilities, re al ists often emphasize state self- interest over these responsibilities in international affairs. C. That is not accurate because critics of humanitarian intervention do not typically over look international law; they often question whether such laws justify intervention or if they can be effectively enforced. D. All of these options are valid points made by critic s of humanitarian intervention, including realists. So the correct answer is D.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 30, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1947", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is D. E osinophilic o sophagitis benefits from anti acid therapy.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
