{"id": "z2203", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 18, "onset_chunk": 18, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is D. In a perfectly competitive industry, firms are price takers, meaning they cannot influence the market price. As a result, the price per unit sold remains constant regardless of the quantity produced. Since average revenue is total revenue divided by quantity, and marginal revenue is the additional revenue from selling one more unit, both will equal the market price in perfect competition. So, average revenue equals marginal revenue.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
